1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
I can’t tell my family what I want without feeling
ungrateful.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:09,000
Private reflection you can correct before exploring peer
experiences.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,100
A local example offers a possibility, not an answer.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,600
Arjun says, Not quite.

5
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:19,900
He changes the words: it is his parents, and he wants time.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,400
Now the editable reflection changes with what he said.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:27,650
He wants time to decide, without advice to stay or leave.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Planned Muse Spark may organize themes to review, never
decide what is true.

9
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,925
Day four: one member wants time to choose.

10
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,200
Another member sees a different part of the situation.

11
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:02,000
Day nine. The host says, I can listen; I can’t decide for
you.

12
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:06,200
Fictional historical examples, prepared and not live.

13
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:16,890
The alias and group audience stay visible.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,660
Private conversation and context are excluded.

15
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:25,100
Consent is unchecked. Continue stays disabled.

16
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:28,000
Nothing is sent from this preview.

17
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,890
He keeps time to decide privately.

18
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,250
He could leave without sharing anything.

19
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:58,810
Maybe later keeps that choice open.

20
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:02,580
Private reflection stays out of the group draft.

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,305
Arjun keeps the next step in his hands.

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Nothing is sent without consent. Arjun can leave it here.

